      "filename": "Afghanistan Camp Russell Memorial, Australian War Memorial.jpg",
      "title": "File:Afghanistan Camp Russell Memorial, Australian War Memorial.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/8f/Afghanistan_Camp_Russell_Memorial%2C_Australian_War_Memorial.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Afghanistan_Camp_Russell_Memorial,_Australian_War_Memorial.jpg",
      "width": 4000,
      "height": 2252,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 4.0",
      "licenseUrl": "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0",
      "artist": "Shkuru Afshar",
      "credit": "Own work",
      "source": "Afghanistan Camp Russell Memorial, Australian War Memorial",
      "description": "Afghanistan Camp Russell Memorial, Australian War MemorialThe sign reads: Memorial from Camp Russell Uruzgan province, Afghanistan\nAustralians first deployed to Afghanistan in 2001. From 2005 to 2013, most Australian personnel were stationed at Tarin Kot in Uruzgan province.\nThe Australian Special Forces and supporting units were based in Camp Russell. The camp was named after the first Australian to be killed in Afghanistan Sergeant Andrew Russell of the Special Air Service Regiment.\nAlthough located within the confines of a larger coalition base (Camp Holland), Camp Russell was a secure and separate enclosure which contained living, medical, and operational facilities. This memorial was the focus for various commemorative ceremonies, such as Anzac Day and Remembrance Day, but was also used during special services held to farewell comrades killed in action.\nThe memorial used for commemorations in Camp Holland - previously displayed on the plinth adjacent to this one - was removed from display in 2020 following damage caused by exposure to weather.\nREL48377\nA member of the Special Operations Engineer Regiment pays tribute on Anzac Day, 25 April 2012.\n\nIMAGE COURTESY OF THE DEPARTMENT OF DEFENCE",
      "dateCreated": "2026-02-11",
      "sourceType": "core",
      "sourceArticleId": "australian-war-memorial-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "r3dp",
      "mediumPath": "_m/r/3/d/p/australian-war-memorial-wp/afghanistan-camp-russe-medium.webp",
      "smallPath": "_m/r/3/d/p/australian-war-memorial-wp/afghanistan-camp-russe-small.webp"
    },
